2-has_title.py::Below are {} pages of a.prompt:
Below are {} pages of a document. Based on these {} pages, determine whether this document contains level-1 titles and level-2 titles.
Note: Sentence-initial enumerative guides such as "first, second, third...", "for one thing, for another..." etc., no matter whether numbered or not, are only logical sequencing phrases within the body text and should NOT be considered as titles.
Given text: 
Page 1{} 
Page 2{} 
Page 3{}
Page 4{}
Return the following JSON format:
{{
    "has_level1_titles": "yes or no",
    "has_level2_titles": "yes or no",
    "reasoning": "Why you think titles exist or not, 300 word explanation"
}}

3-clear_noise.py::Below is one page of a.prompt:
Below is one page of a document. Based on this page, determine whether it contains a table of contents / page-number index (e.g., abundant "numbers", "leader dots", "dotted lines", "ellipses", "guide lines", etc.).
Note: standalone page numbers appearing in headers/footers do NOT count as a table of contents index.
Given text: 
"{page}" 
Return the following JSON format:
{{
    "answer": "yes or no",
    "reasoning": "Why you think this page does or does not contain a catalog/table-of-contents-like page-number index, 300 word explanation"
}}

